        "human",
        "animal"
      ],
      "n": 3000,
      "n_counts": "drugs",
      "verbatim": "In this regard, we recently showed, by producing Likelihood Ratios (LRs) for an extensive data set of over 3,000 drugs with both animal and human data, that the absence of toxicity in animals provides little or virtually no evidential weight that adverse drug reactions will also be absent in humans."
    },
    {
      "statistic": "Likelihood Ratios (LRs)",
      "value": null,
      "unit": "other",
      "measures": "the evidential weight for risk of toxicity in another species when toxicity is present in one species",
      "compared": "presence of toxicity in one species vs risk of toxicity in another species",
      "species": [
        "animal",
        "animal"
      ],
      "n": null,
      "n_counts": null,
      "verbatim": "While our analyses suggest that the presence of toxicity in one species may sometimes add evidential weight for risk of toxicity in another, the LRs are extremely inconsistent, varying substantially for different classes of drugs."
    },
    {
      "statistic": "evidential weight",
      "value": 0,
      "unit": "other",
      "measures": "the evidential weight for toxicity in any other species when test results infer an absence of toxicity in one species",
      "compared": "absence of toxicity in one species vs toxicity in another species",
      "species": [
        "animal",
        "animal"
      ],
      "n": null,
      "n_counts": null,
      "verbatim": "and also show in particular that test results inferring an absence of toxicity in one species provide no evidential weight with regard to toxicity in any other species, even when data from NHPs and humans are compared."
    }
  ],
  "headline_index": null,
  "what_the_study_did": "The study analyzed data from animal tests and human data for over 3,000 drugs to assess the predictive value of animal tests for human drug toxicity and safety.",
  "what_it_found": "The study found that the absence of toxicity in animals provides little to no evidence that adverse drug reactions will be absent in humans, and that test results inferring an absence of toxicity in one species provide no evidential weight regarding toxicity in any other species.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
